      "description": "Watch Anderlecht vs RAAL La Louvière highlights and goals from Jupiler Pro League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 10, 2026. The Jupiler Pro League clash on August 10, 2026, between RSC Anderlecht and RAAL La Louvière delivered a narrative full of tactical shifts and high-stakes tension. Both sides stepped onto the pitch looking to assert their dominance in a match that kept the fans guessing until the very final whistle. A Cautious Opening Half The match began with a display of physical intent, highlighted as early as the 5th minute when Mame Wade of RAAL received a yellow card. Throughout the first half, scoring opportunities remained scarce as both defenses stood firm. Anderlecht attempted to control the rhythm, but the visitors remained disciplined, ensuring the game went into the break without a breakthrough from either side. Breakthrough and a Costly Red Card The second half ignited in the 55th minute when Mustapha Isah found the net to give RAAL La Louvière a surprising lead. However, the momentum shifted decisively just moments later. Joel Ito , who had been cautioned in the 52nd minute, received a second yellow card in the 59th minute and was sent off. This left the visitors to defend their narrow lead with only ten men for the final half-hour. Late Drama and Stoppage-Time Glory Capitalizing on the extra man, RSC Anderlecht intensified their offensive pressure. Their persistence paid off in the 69th minute when Joshua Nga Kana leveled the score, assisted by Ali Maamar . As the clock ticked into stoppage time, the home side found their winner. In the 90+2nd minute, Adriano Bertaccini struck the decisive goal to complete the comeback. Although Bertaccini received a yellow card shortly after for his celebrations, the stadium erupted as Anderlecht secured all three points."
